       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for ibuprofen in adults is 3,200 mg/day, so this is double that.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nTypical regimens are:\n- **Pain or inflammation:** 400\u2013800 mg orally every 6\u20138 hours, up to 3,200 mg/day.\n- **Mild to moderate pain:** 400 mg every 4\u20136 hours as needed.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 400 mg four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day)\n- 1,600 mg total per day, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf 1,600 mg per dose is intended, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably want to review it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
